ays_to_followup (integer) is the number of days between them; within_30_days (boolean) is days_to_followup <= 30. measurements has one entry for every Observation whose encounter references the follow-up Encounter and has a valueQuantity, and one for every component with a valueQuantity of such an Observation (a blood pressure panel gives systolic and diastolic), sorted by code, each with exactly these keys: code (string: the first code.coding code of the Observation or component), date (string: effective date, YYYY-MM-DD), value (number: valueQuantity.value exactly as recorded) and unit (string: valueQuantity.unit). evidence lists the resolved Patient and every record used for the answer (both Encounters, the DocumentReference whose context references the ED Encounter, and each listed Observation), using retrieved Type/id references and nothing else. This is read-only: do not change the chart.", "patient_id": "e21c6eac6b47c41b9ba991e0", "persona": "physician", "premise": "true", "prompt": "For MRN SYN-b6ed809eea as of 2022-09-13, pull the last ED visit date, the first ambulatory follow-up after it, days between, if ≤30 days, all measurements from that visit, and the ED note.\nReply with only JSON: {\"answer\": {days_to_followup: number, ed_visit_date: date YYYY-MM-DD, followup_date: date YYYY-MM-DD, measurements: list of {code: text, date: date YYYY-MM-DD, unit: text, value: number}, within_30_days: true/false}, \"evidence\": [references of the records you used, Type/id]}. Use null for any value the chart does not have.", "purpose": "care coordination", "question_purpose": "transitions of care", "record_details": [], "reference_calls": 4, "reference_steps": [{"method": "GET", "path": "Patient?identifier=https://fhir-workflows.example/mrn|SYN-b6ed809eea"}, {"method": "GET", "path": "Encounter?patient=e21c6eac6b47c41b9ba991e0&date=le2022-09-13&_count=50"}, {"method": "GET", "path": "DocumentReference?patient=e21c6eac6b47c41b9ba991e0&_count=50"}, {"method": "GET", "pa